5738, \"displayName\": \"SLC35A1 exchanges CMP-Neu5Ac for CMP\", \"followingEvent\": [10651552], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"SLC35A1 exchanges CMP-Neu5Ac for CMP\", \"CMP-N-acetyl-beta-neuraminate(in) + CMP(out) = CMP-N-acetyl-beta-neuraminate(out) + CMP(in)\", \"SLC35A1 mediates the antiport of CMP-sialic acid in exchange for CMP\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-727807\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-727807.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"DRE\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 68323, \"displayName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"name\": [\"Danio rerio\", \"D.rerio\", \"D. rerio\", \"Dr\", \"Brachydanio rerio\", \"zebrafish\", \"zebra fish\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"7955\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-9844860\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-9844860.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9990864, \"displayName\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\"}]}"
