l-CoA\", \"Tetracosapentaenoyl-CoA\", \"24:5n-6\"], \"producedByEvent\": [10607715], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-2046055\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-2046055.4\"}, {\"className\": \"Chemical Compound\", \"dbId\": 5228339, \"displayName\": \"Pi [endoplasmic reticulum membrane]\", \"inDisease\": false, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Pi\", \"hydrogenphosphate\", \"Orthophosphate\", \"Phosphate\", \"Inorganic Phosphate\"], \"producedByEvent\": [10607715], \"referenceType\": \"ReferenceMolecule\", \"schemaClass\": \"SimpleEntity\", \"stId\": \"R-ALL-5228339\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-ALL-5228339.5\"}], \"precedingEvent\": [{\"category\": \"transition\", \"className\": \"Reaction\", \"dbId\": 10607723, \"displayName\": \"Desaturation of tetracosatetraenoyl-CoA to tetracosapentaenoyl-CoA\", \"followingEvent\": [10607715], \"isInDisease\": false, \"isInferred\": true, \"maxDepth\": 1, \"name\": [\"Desaturation of tetracosatetraenoyl-CoA to tetracosapentaenoyl-CoA\"], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-2046097\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-2046097.1\"}], \"releaseDate\": \"2026-06-17\", \"schemaClass\": \"Reaction\", \"species\": [{\"abbreviation\": \"DRE\", \"className\": \"Species\", \"dbId\": 68323, \"displayName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"name\": [\"Danio rerio\", \"D.rerio\", \"D. rerio\", \"Dr\", \"Brachydanio rerio\", \"zebrafish\", \"zebra fish\"], \"schemaClass\": \"Species\", \"taxId\": \"7955\"}], \"speciesName\": \"Danio rerio\", \"stId\": \"R-DRE-2046093\", \"stIdVersion\": \"R-DRE-2046093.1\", \"summation\": [{\"className\": \"Summation\", \"dbId\": 9990864, \"displayName\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\", \"schemaClass\": \"Summation\", \"text\": \"This event has been computationally inferred from an event that has been demonstrated in another species.<p>The inference is based on the homology mapping from PANTHER. Briefly, reactions for which all involved PhysicalEntities (in input, output and catalyst) have a mapped orthologue/paralogue (for complexes at least 75% of components must have a mapping) are inferred to the other species. High level events are also inferred for these events to allow for easier navigation.<p><a href='/electronic_inference_compara.html' target = 'NEW'>More details and caveats of the event inference in Reactome.</a> For details on PANTHER see also: <a href='http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp' target='NEW'>http://www.pantherdb.org/about.jsp</a>\"}]}"
